    "text": "<p>We have three aqueous solutions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> labelled as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>‘</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>’</mo><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>‘</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>’</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>‘</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>’</mo></math> with concentration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>,</mo></math> respectively. The value of van <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>’</mo></math> Haft factor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math> for these solutions will be in the order.</p>"
